 "note": "Interaction chains (Ben, 2026-09-10): a spoken line invites replies from ROLES, each reply an atom from the replier's own library. The runner composes: opener -> hop 1 -> hop 2 ..., one line at a time, rolling first_hop_p * decay^(hop-1); a chain dies at max_hops or when the turn changes. Roles: target = the seat(s) the opener addressed (from the event), aggressor = the seat that caused the opener's grief, bystander = another voiced seat, leader = the highest-life other seat, origin = the chain's first speaker (hops >= 2). Nobody replies to themselves; nobody says the same line twice in a turn. Tuned after game 39: no single reply type may dominate — the bystander scoff was five openers' default and became a tic. Ben (game 41): responses and counter-responses must be tight in wall-clock — gap_s 0.25 from the end of the previous line, and the runner polls every 0.1 s while an exchange is pending — a retort lands in 0.25–0.35 s (Ben, game 42). Patter (2026-09-10): board-state, pace and filler lines are addressed to a target the runner picked, so the same table answers them. Round 31 (game 45 measured: 53 % of lines were banter replies, 4 % were about the game): the reply-to-reply and filler invites are pruned to one or two each so an exchange is short unless a board event started it; 140 invites -> 90.",
